{
  "dom_id": "step-111275",
  "name": "Example: \n                    Multiplying a Fraction by a Unit Fraction Using a Model",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14130082/assets/82439d51448a442dede4b3965ecbbd2f2daa7b2365ea75c80951478fd10af65c.png)\n\nUse the model above to calculate $\\dfrac{4}{5} \\times \\dfrac{1}{3}.$",
  "worked_solution": "Since we need to multiply by $\\dfrac{1}{\\color{blue}3}$, we split the whole into $\\color{blue}3$ equal parts horizontally.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14130082/assets/a95b378064e6ec2ed15637fd05ea49e5f988bfb30d8ae788a7b2086ff920a65f.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents $\\dfrac{4}{15}$ of the whole.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{4}{5} \\times \\dfrac{1}{3} = \\dfrac{4}{15}.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
